 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-019\", \"clauses\": {\"compare\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"Compare the numbers: {a} ___ {b}. Which sign is correct: >, <, or =?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 opens with the task word Compare and asks the learner to fill a comparison sign between two generated numbers a and b. Its declared bounds cover the task_type compare_pair variant.\"}, \"two_numbers\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"Compare the numbers: {a} ___ {b}. Which sign is correct: >, <, or =?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 prints exactly two numbers, a and b, in each problem.\"}, \"up_to_20\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"Compare the numbers: {a} ___ {b}. Which sign is correct: >, <, or =?\", \"reasoning\": \"The printed_runs for a and b on F16 span 1 to 20, with no value outside 1 to 20 in the domain.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F06\", \"F07\", \"F12\", \"F20\", \"F21\", \"F23\", \"F24\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"{actor} has {a} {a_word}. {friend} has {b} {b_word}. Which statement is true?\", \"{a} > {neighbour}\", \"{a} {s} {b}\", \"{q} The answer is {v}.\", \"{statement}. True or False?\", \"{actor} is thinking of a number of {objects} that is greater than {a} but less than {b}. What is the number?\", \"{actor} has {a} {objects}. Another classmate has {b} {objects}. Which comparison is correct: {a} ___ {b}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F06: the a_word and b_word slots draw singular and plural nouns from one list with no tie to the counts a and b (template_chosen_by_values does not include them, and distinct_in_every_render is false). Any count of 1 can print a plural noun, and any count above 1 can print a singular one, which is a grammar error for grade 1. F07: the neighbour slot is arithmetic from a with no fixed direction, so the template a > neighbour can print a true statement (neighbour one below a) as an answer choice, which gives the learner a second correct option. F12: the s slot is drawn from all three comparison signs with no link to a or b, so a distractor can print a true comparison that matches the keyed pair. F20: the q slot nests F23 or F24, which ask a question, and the v slot is always a comparison sign, so the text reads as a question followed by a sign given as its answer, which is incoherent for the F23 case where the question asks for a number. F21: it appends a True or False question to the F20 text, so an F20 statement yields a question, then an answer sentence, then the True or False prompt, which is incoherent. F23: it prints the words greater than and less than literally. F02 and F03 gate these to bigger than and smaller than for this lc (words_left_out 1), and neither greater than nor less than appears in cumulative_vocab. The a and b slots are independent, so a pair with no whole number between them (or with a above b) can print an impossible question. The objects drawn from OBJECTS_POOL include gacha tickets, gem tokens, donation cards and subscriber badges, a fandom, gaming and monetization context beyond a grade 1 learner. F24: it draws from the same OBJECTS_POOL with the same context problem, and the word comparison in its question is not in cumulative_vocab. Passing: F01, F02, F03, F04, F05, F08, F09, F10, F13, F14, F15, F16, F18, F19, F22. F16 uses the word sign, which is not in cumulative_vocab; it is not listed as failing because the sign is the only symbol the question asks for, but this is noted. F18 statement values are all true, and every F15 distractor is false.\"}",
